Choices, one event type in each:
(a) as built — job-updated carries the whole table {ID: true/false} on every change, relays and peers the same shape, no timestamp;
(b) same event, the table becomes presence-proof per ID {ID: {present, at}} — the stamp you assume, apps read the age (the fade later), no new name on the stream, the job keeps its name;
(c) a per-change event presence {ID, present, at} and the job retired — one type too, but a new name every app must learn and migrate to.
I recommend (b). Which?
